    "slug": "terms",
    "title": "Terms of use",
    "html": "<h2>Terms of use</h2>\n<p><strong>Last updated: 3 September 2026 · Capsule for macOS</strong></p>\n<p>Capsule is free, open-source software you download and run yourself. There is no account, no subscription, and no service behind it. These terms cover the software; they are short because there is not much to cover.</p>\n<h3>1. The licence is the agreement</h3>\n<p>Capsule is released under the MIT Licence, in <a href=\"https://github.com/realbakari/Capsule-App/blob/main/LICENSE\">LICENSE</a>. That licence grants your rights to use, copy, modify and distribute the software, and nothing on this page takes any of them away. Where this page and the licence disagree, the licence wins.</p>\n<h3>2. There is no service</h3>\n<p>Capsule does not run servers on your behalf, hold an account for you, or process your data anywhere but your own machine. Nothing here promises uptime, availability or support, because there is nothing to keep up.</p>\n<p>Maintainers answer issues when they can. That is a courtesy, not an obligation.</p>\n<h3>3. What you are responsible for</h3>\n<p>Capsule starts coding agents that read and write files and run commands on your computer, with your permissions. You are responsible for:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>What those agents do, including work you approved, work you approved automatically by choosing a permissive mode, and anything destructive that follows.</li>\n<li>Keeping your own backups. A checkpoint is a convenience, not a backup.</li>\n<li>Having the right to work on the code you point Capsule at.</li>\n<li>Your agreements with the AI providers whose CLIs you use, including their terms, their acceptable-use policies, and their pricing. Capsule holds no credentials for them and is not a party to those agreements.</li>\n<li>Complying with the law where you are, including export controls and any sanctions that apply to you.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Do not use Capsule to break into systems you do not own, to produce material that is unlawful where you are, or to violate someone else's rights.</p>\n<h3>4. Other people's software</h3>\n<p>Capsule drives tools it does not ship: Claude Code, Codex, Grok Build, Gemini CLI, OpenClaw, <code>git</code>, <code>gh</code> and others. Those are their authors' software, under their own licences and terms. Naming them here describes what Capsule can drive. It does not imply that Anthropic, OpenAI, xAI, Google, or anyone else endorses, sponsors or is affiliated with this project.</p>\n<p>Trademarks belong to their owners.</p>\n<h3>5. No warranty</h3>\n<p>The software is provided &quot;as is&quot;, without warranty of any kind, express or implied, including merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose and non-infringement. This restates the MIT Licence, and it is meant literally: it may lose your work, and it has bugs nobody has found yet.</p>\n<h3>6. No liability</h3>\n<p>To the fullest extent the law allows, the authors and copyright holders are not liable for any claim, damages or other liability — including lost work, lost data, lost profits, or business interruption — arising from the software or its use, whether in contract, tort or otherwise, and whether or not they were told such damage was possible.</p>\n<p>Some jurisdictions do not allow limits like these. Where that is so, they apply as far as the law permits and no further, and nothing here limits liability for fraud or for death or personal injury caused by negligence.</p>\n<h3>7. Contributions</h3>\n<p>Contributions you send are offered under the MIT Licence, the same terms as the rest of the project. See <a href=\"https://github.com/realbakari/Capsule-App/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md\">CONTRIBUTING.md</a>.</p>\n<h3>8. Changes</h3>\n<p>These terms may change with a release. The date above changes with them, and the full history is public in the repository. Continuing to use a later version means accepting the terms that shipped with it; you are free to stay on the version you have.</p>\n<h3>9. Contact</h3>\n<p>Questions: <a href=\"https://github.com/realbakari/Capsule-App/issues\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer\">https://github.com/realbakari/Capsule-App/issues</a>.</p>\n<hr />\n<p><em>These terms describe how this project is offered. They are not legal advice. Before publishing them on a website, or if you plan to distribute Capsule inside an organisation or in a regulated setting, have a lawyer read them and add the governing-law and contact details your situation needs — they are deliberately absent rather than guessed at.</em></p>"
